# Witness: two legend sections in one document

A section lookup that returns its first match and never asks whether it was the only one can be
pointed at a decoy. Both sections below publish the nine, so the only thing wrong here is that
there are two of them - which is the condition that makes every other clause in this rule
readable from the wrong table.

## 1. How To Use This File

### Evidence verdicts - set by the author, about evidence

| Mark | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `[MET]` | Demonstrated. |
| `[PART]` | Partly demonstrated. |
| `[UNMET]` | Not discharged. |
| `[N/A]` | Not claimed at this milestone. |

### Review verdicts - set by the reviewer, about their own reading

| Mark | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `[ ]` | Not yet reviewed. |
| `[A]` | Accepted as stated. |
| `[C]` | Accepted with a condition. |
| `[R]` | Rejected. |
| `[?]` | Cannot be judged from what is here. |

